          "path": "_m/d/q/9/h/battle-of-malvern-hill-wp/the-malvern-house.jpg",
          "filename": "The Malvern House.jpg",
          "caption": "The Malvern House, General Porter's headquarters during the Battle of Malvern Hill. Original caption:\n\"THE MALVERN HOUSE. FROM A PHOTOGRAPH TAKEN IN\n1885.\n\nDuring the engagement at Turkey bridge and the battle of Malvern Hill, this house was the headquarters of General Porter, and was a signal-station in communication with the gun-boats in the James River, toward which it fronts. It was built of imported English brick, of a dark but vivid red. The main battle-field is in the direction of the trees on the right, and Tyler's siege-guns were near the small trees in the left distance.— Editors\"",
          "alt": "The Malvern House, General Porter's headquarters during the Battle of Malvern Hill. Original caption:\n\"THE MALVERN HOUSE. FROM A PHOTOGRAPH TAKEN IN\n1885.\n\nDuring the engagement at Turkey bridge and the battle of Malvern Hill, this house was the headquarters of General Porter, and was a signal-station in communication with the gun-boats in the James River, toward which it fronts. It was built of imported English brick, of a dark but vivid red. The main battle-field is in the direction of the trees on the right, and Tyler's siege-guns were near the small trees in the left distance.— Editors\"",
          "width": 1594,
          "height": 1339,
